# 2. SPRINT 19 OBJECTIVE

Build a formal **Agent Platform / Agent Capability Framework**.

The system currently has runtime agents and execution infrastructure.

Sprint 19 must establish a standardized contract describing:

WHAT an agent IS
WHAT an agent CAN DO
WHAT tools an agent MAY USE
WHAT execution modes it supports
WHAT lifecycle state it is in
WHAT permissions it requires
WHAT limits apply
HOW it is registered
HOW it is activated/deactivated
HOW the runtime safely resolves and executes it

The target architecture becomes:

```
                AGENT PLATFORM

                     │
          ┌──────────┴──────────┐
          │                     │
   Agent Definition       Agent Lifecycle
          │                     │
   Capabilities            State Machine
          │                     │
   Permissions             Activation
          │                     │
   Tool Access             Deactivation
          │                     │
   Execution Modes         Health
          │                     │
          └──────────┬──────────┘
                     │
               Agent Registry
                     │
                AG-001 Runtime
                     │
         ┌───────────┼───────────┐
         │           │           │
       LLM         AG-002      AG-003
    Reasoning      Memory     Knowledge
                     │
                   AG-004
                    Tools
```

