Create a strongly typed agent definition.

The exact location and naming should follow existing project conventions.

Conceptually an agent definition should support:

* agent ID
* name
* version
* description
* team
* category
* status
* capabilities
* execution modes
* allowed tools
* required permissions
* limits
* dependencies
* configuration
* health metadata

Example conceptual structure:

AgentDefinition

{
id,
name,
version,
description,
team,
category,
status,
capabilities,
executionModes,
allowedTools,
permissions,
limits,
dependencies
}

Use strict TypeScript.

Use Zod for runtime validation.

Do not use `any`.

Do not leak provider-specific types.

